From: illumos-drm <illumos-drm@code.aopc.cloud>
Subject: [PATCH 17] i915: an address space's reservation is initialised once on illumos

Linux initialises the reservation of the GGTT and of every PPGTT twice:
ggtt_probe_hw() and ppgtt_init() call dma_resv_init(&vm->_resv), and
i915_address_space_init(), which follows, calls it again. On Linux the
second init of the still idle reservation is harmless. The facade's
dma_resv_init() keeps the first reservation and warns on a second, so an
attach warned once for every address space it set up (on Ivy Bridge and
Haswell the GGTT, the aliasing PPGTT and the migration context's PPGTT
from intel_migrate_init()), and full-PPGTT hardware once more for each
PPGTT created later.

On illumos i915_address_space_init() leaves vm->_resv to its caller, and
i915_dpt_create(), the one caller that did not initialise it first, does
so before it. Every address space is then initialised once and finished
once, as before: the GGTT by i915_ggtt_driver_late_release() (or the
ggtt_probe_hw() error path), PPGTT and DPT by i915_vm_resv_release().

License: the hunks are trivial preprocessor guards on MIT Linux files;
this patch is applied to the pinned Linux tree, not part of illumos-drm's
sources.

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/gt/intel_gtt.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/gt/intel_gtt.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/gt/intel_gtt.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/gt/intel_gtt.c
@@ -295,7 +295,16 @@ void i915_address_space_init(struct i915_address_space *vm, int subclass)
 		might_alloc(GFP_KERNEL);
 		mutex_release(&vm->mutex.dep_map, _THIS_IP_);
 	}
+#ifndef __illumos__
 	dma_resv_init(&vm->_resv);
+#else
+	/*
+	 * The caller has initialised vm->_resv (ggtt_probe_hw(), ppgtt_init(),
+	 * i915_dpt_create()). The facade's dma_resv_init() keeps the first
+	 * reservation and warns on a second init; on Linux a re-init of the
+	 * idle reservation is harmless.
+	 */
+#endif
 
 	GEM_BUG_ON(!vm->total);
 	drm_mm_init(&vm->mm, 0, vm->total);
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/i915_dpt.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/i915_dpt.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/i915_dpt.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/i915_dpt.c
@@ -229,6 +229,13 @@ static struct intel_dpt *i915_dpt_create(struct drm_gem_object *obj, size_t size
 	vm->total = (size / sizeof(gen8_pte_t)) * I915_GTT_PAGE_SIZE;
 	vm->is_dpt = true;
 
+#ifdef __illumos__
+	/*
+	 * i915_address_space_init() leaves vm->_resv to its caller; GGTT
+	 * and PPGTT initialise it before it, too.
+	 */
+	dma_resv_init(&vm->_resv);
+#endif
 	i915_address_space_init(vm, VM_CLASS_DPT);
 
 	vm->insert_page = dpt_insert_page;
